Distinguish airways from blood vessels. They must never be incorrectly connected.

Allow the user to select pulmonary artery branches and navigate to their associated obstruction models.

Provide a posterior, anterior, lateral, superior, inferior, and free-orbit view.

## Scale B — Pulmonary Artery Geometry

Transition into a selected artery.

Render:

- Vascular lumen.
- Vessel wall.
- Local curvature.
- Bifurcation geometry.
- A model of embolus position.
- Residual flow channels.
- Proximal and distal vascular regions.
- Occluded and partially patent configurations.

