Data may contain:

- Velocity vectors.
- Pressure fields.
- Wall shear stress.
- Flow rates.
- Time-dependent boundary conditions.
- Vessel geometry.
- Solver provenance.

Render the data using color-mapped surfaces, streamlines, slices, and vector glyphs.

Support VTK-compatible preprocessing and suitable GPU-friendly representations.

## Level 3 — Advanced Coupled Simulation

Reserve an optional architecture for coupling modeled clot geometry, vascular geometry, flow, and structural deformation.

This requires a validated physical model and appropriate computational solver.

Do not attempt to substitute decorative GPU particle animations for real CFD.

Do not calculate diagnostic pulmonary artery pressures from appearance alone.

## Visual flow tools

Allow users to:

- Select upstream and downstream regions.
- View flow direction.
- Visualize imported velocity magnitude.
- Create virtual cross-sectional planes.
- Inspect regions of recirculation where supported.
- Compare models with different obstruction levels.
- Display time-resolved streamlines.

Every metric must identify whether it is measured, imported, or simulated.

