# 20. FIBRIN NETWORK GRAPH SCHEMA

Represent the fibrin structure independently of its visual mesh.

```ts
interface FibrinNode {
  id: string;
  position: [number, number, number];
  nodeType: "endpoint" | "junction" | "interior";
}

interface FibrinEdge {
  id: string;
  fromNodeId: string;
  toNodeId: string;
  diameterUm?: number;
  fiberClass?: string;
  crossLinked?: boolean;
}

interface FibrinNetwork {
  id: string;
  seed?: number;
  nodes: FibrinNode[];
  edges: FibrinEdge[];
  evidenceType: EvidenceType;
  modelVersion: string;
}
```

Keep graph structure separate from rendering buffers.

This allows connectivity analysis, reproducible geometry generation, graph-based degradation experiments, and higher-quality scientific validation.

