The user can open the application, explore transparent lungs, select an embolus, navigate into its vessel, isolate a procedural fibrin mesh, manipulate the modeled structure, toggle clot components, control a timeline, inspect data provenance, and enter a compatible immersive 3D mode.

Every core feature must be operational, and the application must visibly distinguish scientific data from experimental or illustrative representations.

**The product succeeds when pulmonary embolism becomes a navigable, layered, scientifically interpretable 3D research environment—not simply an impressive medical animation.**